WEBVTT

00:00:10.090 --> 00:00:12.360
<i>So I'll be back in Japan for the first time in half a year, huh?</i>

00:00:13.190 --> 00:00:16.200
<i>At about the time when the Pennant Race will reach its conclusion.</i>

00:01:57.500 --> 00:01:58.760
Number 7:

00:01:58.760 --> 00:02:01.290
Catcher, Sato.

00:02:02.010 --> 00:02:03.970
Toshi-kun!

00:02:04.680 --> 00:02:06.440
Toshi-kun!

00:02:06.440 --> 00:02:08.520
We're counting on you to hit a big one, Sato!

00:02:08.960 --> 00:02:12.920
Well then, it's the bottom half of the ninth inning. The Tokyo Warriors have gotten runners on that could signal a comeback.

00:02:12.920 --> 00:02:15.940
Sato, who has reached base on two hits safely today, enters the batter's box.

00:02:16.340 --> 00:02:20.410
They only need one more win to take the championship in this three-game series against the Blue Oceans.

00:02:20.410 --> 00:02:22.800
This is their second match, having lost their first one.

00:02:22.800 --> 00:02:26.890
They have to put this chance of a game-ending home run to good use and win the championship!

00:02:32.210 --> 00:02:33.440
<i>Here we go.</i>

00:02:37.200 --> 00:02:38.910
<i>We've got runners on first and second.</i>

00:02:38.910 --> 00:02:39.880
<i>At the very least,</i>

00:02:39.880 --> 00:02:41.970
<i>I have to allow the runners to advance!</i>

00:03:05.890 --> 00:03:06.830
Out!

00:03:08.780 --> 00:03:09.910
Out!

00:03:10.630 --> 00:03:12.020
Game over!

00:03:12.540 --> 00:03:14.340
The game is over!

00:03:14.340 --> 00:03:16.930
In the end the Oceans turned a double play, stranding three players on base.

00:03:16.930 --> 00:03:18.460
And the Oceans win again!

00:03:18.920 --> 00:03:22.130
The Warriors championship win is postponed yet again!

00:03:38.110 --> 00:03:39.560
Oh, geez.

00:03:39.560 --> 00:03:42.480
The victory beer is postponed again.

00:03:42.480 --> 00:03:43.890
Don't complain.

00:03:43.890 --> 00:03:46.330
Having to wait for it will just make it taste even better!

00:03:46.330 --> 00:03:48.270
Yeah I know, but still.

00:03:49.250 --> 00:03:52.220
Sato, three hits in a game. You're in good shape!

00:03:52.220 --> 00:03:54.450
Yes, but if we still lose...

00:03:54.450 --> 00:03:55.530
Don't worry.

00:03:55.530 --> 00:03:57.210
We'll earn a nice win tomorrow.

00:03:58.330 --> 00:04:00.710
Also, I can see it in you.

00:04:00.710 --> 00:04:02.190
You'll be the Newcomer King!

00:04:02.190 --> 00:04:03.800
The Newcomer King!

00:04:03.800 --> 00:04:06.640
You didn't start until half way into the season,

00:04:06.980 --> 00:04:10.310
but you're above most players' batting averages. Your .300 is good enough.

00:04:10.990 --> 00:04:13.090
No, not someone like me.

00:04:14.060 --> 00:04:16.060
There's a much more incredible player out there.

00:04:17.060 --> 00:04:18.590
You mean Mayumura?

00:04:18.590 --> 00:04:19.690
Well, you're right.

00:04:19.690 --> 00:04:21.530
That guy's a monster.

00:04:21.960 --> 00:04:27.240
But still, it's ironic to have former teammates competing to be the Newcomer King.

00:04:31.210 --> 00:04:31.910
Sato.

00:04:32.540 --> 00:04:34.390
The coach is calling you.

00:04:34.390 --> 00:04:35.960
Y-Yes, sir!

00:04:38.010 --> 00:04:41.620
Why didn't you go for a home run in your last at-bat?

00:04:42.140 --> 00:04:43.460
At the time,

00:04:43.460 --> 00:04:45.500
I thought I should make sure the next batter could come up.

00:04:47.380 --> 00:04:50.560
You're swinging the bat well, and you've got the power to hit a homer.

00:04:50.560 --> 00:04:56.810
In a situation with just one out remaining, you have to have faith in yourself to finish the game.

00:04:59.160 --> 00:05:00.480
I'm sorry.

00:05:00.480 --> 00:05:02.310
Even if you're a rookie,

00:05:02.310 --> 00:05:04.750
you're one of the Warriors' starting players.

00:05:04.750 --> 00:05:07.650
Show the spirit that's necessary to carry the team!

00:05:07.650 --> 00:05:08.410
Yes, sir!

00:05:09.380 --> 00:05:11.510
I'm moving you up to the sixth batter in our lineup for tomorrow's game.

00:05:13.060 --> 00:05:13.950
What is it?

00:05:13.950 --> 00:05:14.870
Is that not high enough?

00:05:14.870 --> 00:05:15.800
No.

00:05:15.800 --> 00:05:17.140
It's just...

00:05:17.140 --> 00:05:20.330
Tomorrow, Mayumura is predicted to be the opponent's starting pitcher.

00:05:20.330 --> 00:05:22.880
And I've made no hits in eight at-bats against him this season.

00:05:23.750 --> 00:05:26.220
I'm thinking I might let the team down.

00:05:26.220 --> 00:05:28.680
In that case, make sure that you don't let us down.

00:05:30.650 --> 00:05:31.850
I understand.

00:05:32.240 --> 00:05:33.390
Excuse me.

00:05:34.270 --> 00:05:35.770
Sato.

00:05:35.770 --> 00:05:39.220
Take the title of Newcomer King with your own bat!

00:05:41.650 --> 00:05:42.840
Yes, sir!

00:05:48.030 --> 00:05:50.150
<i>Newcomer King, huh?</i>

00:05:53.750 --> 00:05:55.870
Okay, we'll shoot the picture for the front page now.

00:05:55.870 --> 00:05:58.170
Please get lined up, both of you.

00:06:02.020 --> 00:06:03.490
Looking good.

00:06:03.490 --> 00:06:06.510
The battery who won in the Koshien, the two famous rookies!

00:06:06.510 --> 00:06:09.570
Now they're going to bring their flame to the pro stage! Something like that!

00:06:16.310 --> 00:06:18.640
Well done in that match against the Arrows last week.

00:06:18.640 --> 00:06:20.260
You shut them out completely.

00:06:21.290 --> 00:06:24.040
Yakushiji and Kusano are doing their best as well.

00:06:26.410 --> 00:06:27.730
So I...

00:06:27.730 --> 00:06:29.280
can't afford to lose either.

00:06:33.460 --> 00:06:34.610
I've heard...

00:06:34.610 --> 00:06:38.330
that Shigeno is now the closer for the Triple A team, the Memphis Bats.

00:06:38.330 --> 00:06:40.580
Yeah, I heard that too.

00:06:41.260 --> 00:06:43.670
It's Shigeno we're talking about, after all.

00:06:44.100 --> 00:06:46.510
I'm sure he'll fulfill his dream of joining the Majors very soon.

00:06:48.210 --> 00:06:50.210
I'm planning on going too, eventually.

00:06:51.330 --> 00:06:52.390
That guy...

00:06:52.390 --> 00:06:57.020
He refused to go pro, and chose to challenge the Majors instead.

00:06:57.920 --> 00:06:58.850
But...

00:06:58.850 --> 00:07:00.190
I'm different.

00:07:00.190 --> 00:07:02.350
First, I'll become the Newcomer King.

00:07:03.520 --> 00:07:05.030
I'll get the most wins.

00:07:05.030 --> 00:07:06.960
I'll earn the greatest defense ratio.

00:07:06.960 --> 00:07:08.070
I'll become the MVP.

00:07:09.110 --> 00:07:11.530
I'll absorb new skills in pro baseball,

00:07:11.530 --> 00:07:14.490
then I'll take lots of titles, and finally challenge the world.

00:07:15.590 --> 00:07:18.200
After that, I'll have my showdown with Shigeno.

00:07:21.770 --> 00:07:23.390
That's just like you, Mayumura.

00:07:26.850 --> 00:07:28.370
What will you do?

00:07:43.470 --> 00:07:46.390
Toshiya, your breakfast is ready!

00:07:46.390 --> 00:07:48.030
Okay, I'm coming!

00:07:49.260 --> 00:07:51.320
Oh, Toshiya!

00:07:52.170 --> 00:07:53.340
What do you think?

00:07:54.660 --> 00:07:56.110
Warriors...

00:07:56.110 --> 00:07:58.050
victory commemoration sale?

00:07:58.870 --> 00:08:01.100
During the week after you win,

00:08:01.100 --> 00:08:05.830
I'm thinking of lowering the price of all the boxed lunches in the store by 50 yen!

00:08:06.310 --> 00:08:08.680
And we won't stop there!

00:08:08.680 --> 00:08:11.260
Once you've become number one in Japan, we'll have a sale and cut prices by 100 yen!

00:08:11.750 --> 00:08:15.260
And if you become the Newcomer King, everything will be half off!

00:08:17.340 --> 00:08:21.100
If you act that selfishly, the shop manager will be angry with you.

00:08:21.100 --> 00:08:23.170
No, he won't be angry.

00:08:23.170 --> 00:08:25.570
He's a long-time Warriors fan.

00:08:25.570 --> 00:08:28.450
I'm happy about what you're doing, but please don't overexert yourselves.

00:08:28.450 --> 00:08:29.270
Don't worry.

00:08:29.270 --> 00:08:31.300
This is the least we can do.

00:08:31.300 --> 00:08:33.790
We have to cheer you on, after all.

00:08:34.360 --> 00:08:35.780
This is fun.

00:08:35.780 --> 00:08:38.850
It's almost as if we're playing baseball together with you, Toshiya!

00:08:39.830 --> 00:08:41.500
Grandpa.

00:08:41.500 --> 00:08:42.630
Grandma.

00:08:43.430 --> 00:08:46.520
I know! Let's make leaflets and give them out in the neighborhood.

00:08:46.520 --> 00:08:48.970
You'll hurt your hip again.

00:08:48.970 --> 00:08:50.600
What are you saying?

00:08:50.600 --> 00:08:53.190
My hip won't get hurt just because of something like this.

00:08:59.540 --> 00:09:02.030
To the Warriors Dome, please.

00:09:10.100 --> 00:09:11.820
<i>What will you do?</i>

00:09:14.330 --> 00:09:15.630
<i>The world, huh?</i>

00:09:15.630 --> 00:09:17.730
<i>To be honest, I haven't thought about that.</i>

00:09:18.390 --> 00:09:21.040
<i>I've always made turning pro my goal.</i>

00:09:21.600 --> 00:09:23.520
<i>And my family is happy.</i>

00:09:24.180 --> 00:09:26.730
<i>And the Warriors' fans are all expecting me to do great things.</i>

00:09:28.490 --> 00:09:31.310
<i>I'll continue playing baseball in Japan.</i>

00:09:31.310 --> 00:09:33.550
<i>Don't you have a will of your own?</i>

00:09:34.380 --> 00:09:37.120
<i>What are you playing baseball for?</i>

00:09:38.220 --> 00:09:40.800
<i>Are you playing to make someone else happy?</i>

00:09:40.800 --> 00:09:43.770
<i>Are you going to stay in the lukewarm bath forever?</i>

00:09:45.050 --> 00:09:46.040
<i>Wait a moment!</i>

00:09:46.040 --> 00:09:49.620
<i>Going up against the world is certainly one available path,</i>

00:09:49.620 --> 00:09:51.980
<i>but that's not all there is, you know?</i>

00:09:51.980 --> 00:09:55.860
<i>Taking your path is definitely easier than throwing away all of your achievements,</i>

00:09:55.860 --> 00:09:57.910
<i>and going alone to the unknown that is America.</i>

00:09:59.980 --> 00:10:01.080
<i>It's a lukewarm bath.</i>

00:10:10.950 --> 00:10:12.290
Toshi-kun!

00:10:13.620 --> 00:10:14.840
I'll get out here.

00:10:16.620 --> 00:10:17.900
Toshi-kun!

00:10:17.900 --> 00:10:19.150
Toshi-kun!

00:10:20.770 --> 00:10:22.680
What do you think it is,

00:10:22.680 --> 00:10:23.850
that Sato lacks?

00:10:27.640 --> 00:10:30.020
What he lacks?

00:10:32.040 --> 00:10:33.240
It's greed.

00:10:33.240 --> 00:10:34.070
Greed?

00:10:34.620 --> 00:10:36.880
He became a pro in the first draft.

00:10:36.880 --> 00:10:38.680
And also became a starting player.

00:10:39.190 --> 00:10:41.750
After achieving his dream,

00:10:41.750 --> 00:10:44.030
he no longer has an objective.

00:10:44.620 --> 00:10:45.880
Last night,

00:10:45.880 --> 00:10:48.210
his decision to try and pass the chance along to the next batter wasn't wrong.

00:10:49.030 --> 00:10:51.430
To tell a rookie to pull the whole team by himself,

00:10:51.430 --> 00:10:53.500
might be a bit too much to ask for.

00:10:54.030 --> 00:10:55.140
But,

00:10:55.140 --> 00:10:58.670
I don't want him to be satisfied with just this.

00:11:01.520 --> 00:11:04.080
I want him to be more greedy, so he'll train harder.

00:11:04.900 --> 00:11:05.510
This boy...

00:11:06.240 --> 00:11:09.200
will be one of the men that carries the Japanese baseball world on his shoulders in the future!

00:11:15.180 --> 00:11:17.720
If you win today, it'll be your tenth win.

00:11:17.720 --> 00:11:21.610
And, you've been completely shutting out your rival, Sato, as well.

00:11:21.980 --> 00:11:24.860
If this continues, you'll become the Newcomer King for sure.

00:11:26.370 --> 00:11:28.850
Still, don't drop your guard.

00:11:28.850 --> 00:11:32.060
Especially with the heavy-hitting Rodman.

00:11:32.060 --> 00:11:34.040
He's the current Home Run King, after all.

00:11:35.010 --> 00:11:36.210
Rodman?

00:11:36.210 --> 00:11:37.630
What?

00:11:37.630 --> 00:11:39.510
Why do you look so surprised?

00:11:39.510 --> 00:11:42.520
Are you implying that Rodman's no threat?

00:11:42.520 --> 00:11:43.690
He isn't.

00:11:49.730 --> 00:11:54.730
This is a free fansub.

00:11:49.730 --> 00:11:54.730
Not for sale or rent.

00:11:56.440 --> 00:11:57.730
Strike!

00:11:59.650 --> 00:12:02.110
So they've brought out Kamihira, their ace.

00:12:02.110 --> 00:12:04.370
They're desperate too.

00:12:04.370 --> 00:12:06.720
This'll be a pitcher's battle.

00:12:06.720 --> 00:12:08.370
We're counting on you, Mayumura!

00:12:10.540 --> 00:12:12.250
Where did he go?

00:12:12.250 --> 00:12:14.790
He's probably getting focused.

00:12:14.790 --> 00:12:17.560
Oh yeah, that ceremony of his.

00:12:30.600 --> 00:12:32.020
Strike! Batter out!

00:12:33.360 --> 00:12:35.360
Strike! Batter out!

00:12:36.690 --> 00:12:38.070
Number 3:

00:12:38.070 --> 00:12:40.450
Right-hander, Rodman.

00:12:40.450 --> 00:12:42.150
Come on, rookie!

00:12:48.520 --> 00:12:50.120
Strike!

00:12:51.770 --> 00:12:53.000
Strike two!

00:12:56.360 --> 00:12:58.460
<i>Even though you're called Home Run King,</i>

00:12:58.900 --> 00:13:03.130
<i>you only have that title from going up against second-rate pitchers.</i>

00:13:04.160 --> 00:13:06.680
<i>Really, you're just...</i>

00:13:06.680 --> 00:13:07.930
<i>a fake!</i>

00:13:10.740 --> 00:13:11.720
Strike!

00:13:11.720 --> 00:13:13.560
Batter out!

00:13:17.530 --> 00:13:19.460
His pitches are sharp today as well.

00:13:19.460 --> 00:13:20.440
Yeah.

00:13:22.750 --> 00:13:24.360
<i>Do you remember?</i>

00:13:26.960 --> 00:13:29.070
<i>The first match I played against you,</i>

00:13:29.070 --> 00:13:31.870
<i>was when the scholarship student team played the Dream Island team.</i>

00:13:33.110 --> 00:13:34.840
<i>That time,</i>

00:13:34.840 --> 00:13:36.670
<i>you came from Dream Island,</i>

00:13:37.110 --> 00:13:39.610
<i>and desperately tried to win.</i>

00:13:39.610 --> 00:13:41.590
<i>You were trying to acquire the role of starting catcher.</i>

00:13:43.050 --> 00:13:44.880
<i>That tenacity of yours...</i>

00:13:44.880 --> 00:13:49.220
<i>blasted my full-strength gyroball all the way to the backstop, remember?</i>

00:13:51.660 --> 00:13:55.080
<i>"Eventually, I'd like to fight this guy for real."</i>

00:13:55.080 --> 00:13:57.980
<i>The only ones who thought that were you and Shigeno.</i>

00:13:59.180 --> 00:14:02.390
<i>I thought you were the one who wanted to fight...</i>

00:14:02.390 --> 00:14:04.400
<i>against Shigeno the most,</i>

00:14:04.890 --> 00:14:08.290
<i>but if you're going to stay in the lukewarm bath, I won't stop you.</i>

00:14:09.600 --> 00:14:11.930
<i>I'll be the one to become the Newcomer King!</i>

00:14:13.100 --> 00:14:14.560
<i>Against the current you,</i>

00:14:14.560 --> 00:14:16.580
<i>I know I won't lose!</i>

00:14:19.680 --> 00:14:21.540
Strike! Batter out!

00:14:25.900 --> 00:14:27.800
<i>The one who will stay in Japan,</i>

00:14:28.190 --> 00:14:29.840
<i>and the one who will aim for the world.</i>

00:14:32.540 --> 00:14:35.950
<i>Is it because of the difference in our goals that I can't hit off him?</i>

00:14:37.430 --> 00:14:39.980
Sato struck out in his second at-bat as well!

00:14:39.980 --> 00:14:43.310
They are former teammates who are now competing for the Newcomer King title,

00:14:43.310 --> 00:14:44.530
but Shigeno-san,

00:14:44.530 --> 00:14:47.280
Sato is being completely overwhelmed by Mayumura, wouldn't you say?

00:14:47.280 --> 00:14:48.430
Yeah.

00:14:48.430 --> 00:14:51.460
Mayumura is in great form right now, but that's not all.

00:14:51.460 --> 00:14:54.950
I get the feeling that Sato is uncertain in his at-bats today.

00:14:55.560 --> 00:14:57.810
His swings are uncertain.

00:14:58.360 --> 00:15:00.500
He can't hit like that.

00:15:05.480 --> 00:15:06.290
Strike!

00:15:06.290 --> 00:15:07.550
Batter out!

00:15:07.550 --> 00:15:09.220
Tanioka struck out!

00:15:09.640 --> 00:15:11.530
In the sixth inning, every batter struck out!

00:15:11.530 --> 00:15:16.180
The only runners Mayumura has allowed on base were as a result of an error made by his teammates, and one walk.

00:15:16.180 --> 00:15:19.370
Maybe his tenth win will be a no-hitter!

00:15:19.370 --> 00:15:21.810
His pitching isn't getting weaker,

00:15:21.810 --> 00:15:23.830
so he might actually accomplish that.

00:15:24.530 --> 00:15:27.230
But Kamihira is also shutting out the opposition completely.

00:15:27.740 --> 00:15:30.950
The team that scores first will hold an advantage.

00:15:39.630 --> 00:15:40.520
Out!

00:15:44.550 --> 00:15:45.500
Out!

00:15:46.960 --> 00:15:48.010
<i>In the middle again!</i>

00:15:52.140 --> 00:15:55.720
<i>It seems Kamihira-san has suddenly lost control over his pitches this inning.</i>

00:15:58.590 --> 00:15:59.590
<i>It can't be!</i>

00:16:00.090 --> 00:16:02.020
Time, please!

00:16:02.510 --> 00:16:03.790
Kamihira-san!

00:16:03.790 --> 00:16:05.010
Could it be...

00:16:05.010 --> 00:16:06.820
that your shoulder hurts from last year's injury?

00:16:06.820 --> 00:16:09.980
Yeah, it's straining a little.

00:16:09.980 --> 00:16:12.600
I'm allowing the pain to distract me from making my pitches accurate,

00:16:12.600 --> 00:16:13.950
but I'll be all right now!

00:16:13.950 --> 00:16:16.930
But it would be a disaster if you hurt it again by being too reckless.

00:16:16.930 --> 00:16:18.080
You should sub out.

00:16:18.080 --> 00:16:20.670
Do you think I can leave the mound in this situation?

00:16:20.670 --> 00:16:22.370
Our victory hinges upon me!

00:16:23.900 --> 00:16:26.600
I want to be thrown up into the air for my pitching skills!

00:16:26.600 --> 00:16:28.050
Let me pitch!

00:16:35.580 --> 00:16:37.260
<i>Fastballs won't do the trick here.</i>

00:16:37.760 --> 00:16:39.850
<i>Let's corner him with breaking balls.</i>

00:16:40.280 --> 00:16:41.690
<i>Start with a curveball.</i>

00:16:47.270 --> 00:16:48.570
<i>It's not curving!</i>

00:16:54.400 --> 00:16:55.780
Out!

00:16:57.120 --> 00:17:00.270
Nicely played by Kurogome, well done keeping up!

00:17:00.270 --> 00:17:03.120
The seventh inning ends, and it's still 0-0!

00:17:07.420 --> 00:17:09.640
Strike! Batter out!

00:17:09.640 --> 00:17:12.760
That idiot. He swung too wide again.

00:17:12.760 --> 00:17:14.010
Number 4:

00:17:14.010 --> 00:17:16.020
Third batter, Uchimura!

00:17:16.020 --> 00:17:16.810
Uchimura!

00:17:16.810 --> 00:17:18.100
Give it your all!

00:17:21.050 --> 00:17:23.600
<i>Our relief pitchers are unstable right now.</i>

00:17:24.370 --> 00:17:27.310
<i>Against Mayumura, our chances to win are slim.</i>

00:17:29.180 --> 00:17:29.990
Ball!

00:17:29.990 --> 00:17:30.980
Ball four!

00:17:32.940 --> 00:17:34.810
We'll use a sacrifice bunt here, right?

00:17:34.810 --> 00:17:36.070
Yeah.

00:17:36.070 --> 00:17:37.880
Next up is Sato,

00:17:37.880 --> 00:17:39.330
but do you want to put in a pinch hitter?

00:17:41.780 --> 00:17:42.870
<i>I can't allow...</i>

00:17:42.870 --> 00:17:46.200
<i>Kamihira-san's shoulder to be strained any more.</i>

00:17:47.490 --> 00:17:48.930
<i>This inning,</i>

00:17:48.930 --> 00:17:51.180
<i>we have to win somehow!</i>

00:17:53.300 --> 00:17:55.370
<i>You've only got this shoulder!</i>

00:17:55.370 --> 00:17:56.890
<i>Goro-kun,</i>

00:17:56.890 --> 00:17:58.800
<i>you've only got this shoulder left!</i>

00:18:00.010 --> 00:18:02.320
<i>Together, Goro-kun...</i>

00:18:02.320 --> 00:18:06.020
<i>I want to go to Koshien together with you, as well as everyone else!</i>

00:18:06.540 --> 00:18:07.350
<i>Toshi.</i>

00:18:09.780 --> 00:18:11.280
<i>In that case,</i>

00:18:11.280 --> 00:18:13.020
<i>will you do me a favor?</i>

00:18:14.220 --> 00:18:16.150
<i>Finish it in this inning, will you?</i>

00:18:16.150 --> 00:18:17.580
<i>You're the only one...</i>

00:18:17.580 --> 00:18:18.910
<i>who can hit Mayumura's pitch!</i>

00:18:18.910 --> 00:18:20.540
<i>who can hit Mayumura's pitch!</i>

00:18:20.540 --> 00:18:22.060
<i>who can hit Mayumura's pitch!</i>

00:18:27.530 --> 00:18:28.700
Out!

00:18:32.540 --> 00:18:33.760
Coach!

00:18:34.850 --> 00:18:35.710
Sato!

00:18:38.240 --> 00:18:39.430
Can you do it?

00:18:39.430 --> 00:18:40.600
Yes, sir.

00:18:40.600 --> 00:18:41.880
I will.

00:18:41.880 --> 00:18:43.350
Definitely!

00:18:49.620 --> 00:18:51.440
<i>You're wrong, Mayumura.</i>

00:18:52.400 --> 00:18:56.280
<i>At that time, I wasn't thinking about becoming a regular at all.</i>

00:18:59.170 --> 00:19:01.670
<i>"I want to respond to Goro-kun's wish."</i>

00:19:01.670 --> 00:19:03.740
<i>That feeling helped me.</i>

00:19:03.740 --> 00:19:05.790
<i>That's why I hit that home run!</i>

00:19:09.870 --> 00:19:12.000
<i>It's always been that way.</i>

00:19:13.130 --> 00:19:14.170
<i>In Little League,</i>

00:19:15.500 --> 00:19:16.710
<i>and in middle grade,</i>

00:19:17.970 --> 00:19:25.850
<i>someone has always depended on me, and those feelings have given strength to this bat!</i>

00:19:37.080 --> 00:19:38.030
Foul!

00:19:48.000 --> 00:19:49.460
<i>What's up with this guy?</i>

00:19:49.460 --> 00:19:52.440
<i>Suddenly his swing got a lot better.</i>

00:19:52.440 --> 00:19:54.000
<i>Shall we scare him with curves?</i>

00:19:56.550 --> 00:19:57.380
<i>What!?</i>

00:19:59.970 --> 00:20:03.090
<i>Seems like you've found your answer, Sato.</i>

00:20:03.700 --> 00:20:05.500
<i>That's how it should be.</i>

00:20:05.500 --> 00:20:07.260
<i>Otherwise there wouldn't be any point...</i>

00:20:08.350 --> 00:20:09.770
<i>in returning the favor!</i>

00:20:12.190 --> 00:20:13.440
Strike!

00:20:23.000 --> 00:20:24.000
Foul!

00:20:26.230 --> 00:20:27.300
Foul!

00:20:38.420 --> 00:20:41.340
<i>I've got a rival straight ahead of me, and competing against each other, we'll rise together.</i>

00:20:41.550 --> 00:20:44.680
<i>And then there's the fans and my family cheering for me.</i>

00:20:45.100 --> 00:20:47.850
<i>As well as teammates and coaches that I can trust.</i>

00:20:49.060 --> 00:20:51.280
<i>As long as there are people counting on me,</i>

00:20:51.280 --> 00:20:52.060
<i>I will play,</i>

00:20:54.770 --> 00:20:55.900
<i>here in Japan!</i>

00:21:04.060 --> 00:21:05.400
There it is!

00:21:05.400 --> 00:21:06.900
Home run!

00:21:06.900 --> 00:21:09.830
That two-run home run is priceless!

00:21:09.830 --> 00:21:11.660
The Warriors have more wins than losses!

00:21:11.660 --> 00:21:12.620
Yes!

00:21:12.620 --> 00:21:14.040
Toshiya!

00:21:17.490 --> 00:21:19.360
<i>Before challenging the world,</i>

00:21:19.360 --> 00:21:21.420
<i>you've acquired something else to do, it seems.</i>

00:21:23.380 --> 00:21:24.610
<i>But eventually,</i>

00:21:26.080 --> 00:21:28.680
<i>if I really get in the mood to challenge you,</i>

00:21:30.650 --> 00:21:31.970
<i>that's when I'll go.</i>

00:21:33.990 --> 00:21:35.690
Strike! Batter out!

00:21:36.150 --> 00:21:37.600
Game over!

00:21:38.560 --> 00:21:40.950
The Warriors win!

00:21:40.950 --> 00:21:44.860
Continuing on from last year, they've dominated the Pennant Race!

00:21:57.110 --> 00:21:59.670
The Texas Raiders lose consecutively!

00:21:59.670 --> 00:22:02.670
They were unable to get any closer to winning the championship today.

00:22:02.670 --> 00:22:06.340
Oh, man. What are those guys doing?

00:22:07.860 --> 00:22:10.960
<i>Hurry up and come back, Honda Jr.</i>

00:22:10.960 --> 00:22:15.050
<i>This time I'll crush your 100 mph pitch all the way to the stands!</i>

00:22:15.050 --> 00:22:17.190
Hey, Junior!

00:22:17.570 --> 00:22:19.060
The coach is calling for you!

00:22:20.840 --> 00:22:22.270
I'm being called up!?

00:22:22.270 --> 00:22:23.660
That's right.

00:22:23.660 --> 00:22:25.800
It seems that the Raiders' third baseman...

00:22:25.800 --> 00:22:27.700
has been put on the disabled list.

00:22:28.340 --> 00:22:30.570
Well, it'll be tough for us to lose you,

00:22:30.570 --> 00:22:32.910
but if the upper guys have an emergency, there's not much we can do.

00:22:33.290 --> 00:22:35.550
You're on the first flight to Texas tomorrow morning...

00:22:35.550 --> 00:22:36.800
to join up with them.

00:24:12.200 --> 00:24:16.160
The seventh and final match against the Falcons, with a league victory on the line.

00:24:16.160 --> 00:24:19.890
We'll win this, and take the championship!

00:24:19.890 --> 00:24:20.810
Amidst all this,

00:24:20.810 --> 00:24:22.850
that man has appeared in the stadium!

00:24:22.850 --> 00:24:24.530
Next time, on Major:

00:24:24.530 --> 00:24:26.110
A Great Man.

00:24:26.110 --> 00:24:28.630
Run towards the stage of your dreams!
